abstract: "Kernel methods for stochastic Koopman operators often assume that the dynamics map a Gaussian RKHS into itself. Gaussian transitions N(F(x),Q(x)) between global Gaussian RKHSs force constant Q, affine F and MRM^T <= P+4Q; additive noise with a Gaussian lower bound on its characteristic function (every infinitely divisible law) forces affine drift, and only the Gaussian covariance component counts. A compound-Poisson approximation of a stable linear diffusion converges at sharp order eps^2 in the norm into bounded continuous functions while every approximant sends exp(-8|x|^2/5) outside the RKHS. Ornstein-Uhlenbeck invariance holds exactly when AP+PA^T <= 4BB^T, so the sufficient condition with factor 2 of Philipp et al. (2025) is not necessary; this fixed affine criterion specialises classical Gaussian-Fock theory, and the witness was proposed first in GitHub issue the-omega-institute/trureturing #23376. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
